/*
We are given:
- n vertices, numbered 1..n
- two special vertices a and b
- for each vertex i, distances da[i] = dist(a, i), db[i] = dist(b, i)

We must determine whether there exists a connected undirected graph realizing these distances.
If yes, output the minimum possible number of edges.

Key facts:
1) Let D = dist(a, b). Then for every vertex i:
      |da[i] - db[i]| <= D <= da[i] + db[i]
   and parity:
      da[i] + db[i] ≡ D (mod 2)
   because any shortest path geometry around endpoints a,b induces:
      x = (da[i] + db[i] - D)/2
      t = (da[i] - db[i] + D)/2
   where t is the position on an a-b shortest path, x is distance from i to that path.
   Thus x,t must be nonnegative integers.

2) There must be exactly one vertex with (da,db) = (0,D): vertex a,
   exactly one with (D,0): vertex b,
   and for each t=0..D there must be at least one vertex with x=0 and position t,
   i.e. pair (t, D-t), to form the backbone shortest path from a to b.

3) Every vertex belongs to a "group" (t,x), where:
      t = (da - db + D)/2
      x = (da + db - D)/2
   Vertices with same (t,x) are indistinguishable by distances to a,b.

To minimize edges:
- Need a simple path of length D as backbone: D edges.
- For each position t, vertices with x=0 at that t:
    if count > 1, they cannot be connected among themselves only (would break distances),
    each extra such vertex must attach to some vertex at same t with x=1.
    Therefore for every t with count0[t] > 1, we need at least one vertex at (t,1).
- For x>=1, every vertex in layer x must connect to some vertex in layer x-1 with same t,
  requiring at least count(t,x) edges to give each vertex one parent.
  This is sufficient if there is at least one vertex in previous layer.
- For x=0, among the backbone representatives, one per t is used in the path.
  Extra x=0 vertices need one edge each to layer (t,1).

Hence total minimum edges:
    D
  + sum over all groups with x>=1 of count(t,x)
  + sum over t of (count(t,0)-1)

Subject to existence conditions:
- all vertices produce integral valid (t,x), 0<=t<=D, x>=0
- for every t, count(t,0) >= 1
- if count(t,0) > 1 then count(t,1) >= 1
- for every group (t,x) with x>=1 and count>0, previous group (t,x-1) must exist

This is also sufficient.

We can process by grouping vertices per t and x.
*/

public class Main {
    static class FastScanner {
        private final InputStream in = System.in;
        private final byte[] buffer = new byte[1 << 16];
        private int ptr = 0, len = 0;

        private int read() throws IOException {
            if (ptr >= len) {
                len = in.read(buffer);
                ptr = 0;
                if (len <= 0) return -1;
            }
            return buffer[ptr++];
        }

        int nextInt() throws IOException {
            int c;
            do c = read(); while (c <= ' ' && c != -1);
            int sign = 1;
            if (c == '-') {
                sign = -1;
                c = read();
            }
            int val = 0;
            while (c > ' ') {
                val = val * 10 + (c - '0');
                c = read();
            }
            return val * sign;
        }
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        FastScanner fs = new FastScanner();

        int n = fs.nextInt();
        int a = fs.nextInt() - 1;
        int b = fs.nextInt() - 1;

        int[] da = new int[n];
        int[] db = new int[n];
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) da[i] = fs.nextInt();
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) db[i] = fs.nextInt();

        int D = da[b];

        // Basic endpoint consistency
        if (da[a] != 0 || db[b] != 0 || db[a] != D || da[b] != D) {
            System.out.println(-1);
            return;
        }

        // groups[t] -> map x -> count
        @SuppressWarnings("unchecked")
        HashMap<Integer, Integer>[] groups = new HashMap[D + 1];
        for (int t = 0; t <= D; t++) groups[t] = new HashMap<>();

        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            int sum = da[i] + db[i] - D;
            int diff = da[i] - db[i] + D;

            if ((sum & 1) != 0 || (diff & 1) != 0) {
                System.out.println(-1);
                return;
            }

            int x = sum / 2;
            int t = diff / 2;

            if (x < 0 || t < 0 || t > D) {
                System.out.println(-1);
                return;
            }

            groups[t].put(x, groups[t].getOrDefault(x, 0) + 1);
        }

        long edges = D;

        for (int t = 0; t <= D; t++) {
            int c0 = groups[t].getOrDefault(0, 0);
            if (c0 == 0) {
                System.out.println(-1);
                return;
            }

            // one x=0 vertex at each t is used on the main path
            edges += c0 - 1;

            if (c0 > 1 && groups[t].getOrDefault(1, 0) == 0) {
                System.out.println(-1);
                return;
            }

            // For every x>=1 present, previous layer must exist.
            for (Map.Entry<Integer, Integer> e : groups[t].entrySet()) {
                int x = e.getKey();
                int cnt = e.getValue();
                if (x >= 1) {
                    if (groups[t].getOrDefault(x - 1, 0) == 0) {
                        System.out.println(-1);
                        return;
                    }
                    edges += cnt;
                }
            }
        }

        System.out.println(edges);
    }
}

